    "description": "A combat air patrol (starts at 2x speed). The Pursuer flies a racetrack orbit at 25 000 ft; a Target comes in low and fast from the east at 3 000 ft. The radar only looks ahead, so it can only find the Target on the east-bound leg: watch the cone sweep away and back as the orbit turns. When the track confirms inside the zone the Pursuer fires, then keeps flying its orbit; at the next turn the track and the datalink drop, and the missile, lofted far above, has to fly on its last estimate until its own seeker finds the low Target. A pilot who wants to keep supporting the shot 'cranks' instead: turns only as far as the radar's scan limit.",
